From 4d2f8c1e9b7a65c3f0e1d2b3a4c5d6e7f8a9b0c1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Otavio Morais <otaviomorais@github.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sched/fair: use 4.19 task state in task_change_group_fair

The e404 base (4.19 + sched grafts) keeps the 4.19 task_struct field
`state`, but task_change_group_fair() (compiled only with
CONFIG_FAIR_GROUP_SCHED=y) references the 5.x name `__state`, breaking
the build. TASK_NEW already exists in the grafted sched.h, so the
4.19 spelling compiles cleanly.

Signed-off-by: Otavio Morais <otaviomorais@github.com>
---
 kernel/sched/fair.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/fair.c b/kernel/sched/fair.c
index 8c55b71aa2ef..2359aac6bf1e 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -13497,7 +13497,7 @@ static void task_change_group_fair(struct task_struct *p)
 	 * We couldn't detach or attach a forked task which
 	 * hasn't been woken up by wake_up_new_task().
 	 */
-	if (READ_ONCE(p->__state) == TASK_NEW)
+	if (READ_ONCE(p->state) == TASK_NEW)
 		return;
 
 	detach_task_cfs_rq(p);
